  "term": "state anxiety",
  "definition": "In mental health, state anxiety is the fluctuating, time-varying form of anxiety, described here as the tendency to perceive stressful situations as dangerous or threatening when that tendency changes over time. In this article, it is contrasted with trait anxiety, which is presented as the more stable form.",
